WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.777
In Microsoft Fabric, be careful about which SQL surface you are using.

00:00:04.777 --> 00:00:08.837
A Spark notebook or Spark SQL cell runs through Spark.

00:00:08.837 --> 00:00:16.162
A SQL analytics endpoint uses a different SQL serving surface, often with T-SQL style behavior.

00:00:16.162 --> 00:00:19.142
Some syntax and capabilities differ.

00:00:19.142 --> 00:00:23.917
When code fails, first check which engine you are actually using.

00:00:23.917 --> 00:00:29.257
When reading the example, do not read punctuation one character at a time.

00:00:29.257 --> 00:00:33.837
Start with the purpose of the query, then identify the input rows, the operation being applied,

00:00:33.837 --> 00:00:38.327
and the shape of the expected output.

00:00:38.327 --> 00:00:45.362
In a real setting such as a retail pipeline aggregating high-volume sales data across partitions,

00:00:45.362 --> 00:00:51.517
this habit makes code reviews much easier because you can explain what the query is supposed to guarantee

00:00:51.517 --> 00:00:53.907
before discussing syntax.

00:00:53.907 --> 00:01:00.298
After running it, inspect a few records manually and check that the result matches that explanation.
